<title>UK: UAE tells OPEC it produced 2.1329 mln bpd in April.</title>
<headline>UAE tells OPEC it produced 2.1329 mln bpd in April.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC member the United Arab Emirates (UAE) told the groups secretariat that it produced 2.1329 million barrels of oil per day (bpd) in April, the OPEC news agency OPECNA said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>But the UAE said it had supplied to the market 2.1610 million bpd in April. The UAE's OPEC quota - defined by supply to the market rather wellhead output - is 2.1610 million bpd.</p>
<p>OPEC defines supply as domestic consumption plus net export sales of crude and products plus withdrawals of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>A Reuter survey of analysts and industry sources found that the UAE produced 2.25 million bpd in April.</p>
<p>OPECNA also gave April production and supply figures for the following countries listed below in million bpd: COUNTRY	 PRODUCTION   SUPPLY</p>
<p>---------------------------------</p>
<p>ALGERIA	  0.7990	0.7910</p>
<p>INDONESIA	1.3278	 N.A.</p>
<p>IRAQ	     1.7000	1.7000</p>
<p>KUWAIT	   2.0068	2.0078</p>
<p>LIBYA	    1.3940	1.3950</p>
<p>NIGERIA	  1.8314	1.8649</p>
<p>QATAR	    0.4132	0.3952</p>
<p>SAUDI ARABIA   8.0011	8.0017</p>
<p>UAE		2.1329	2.1610</p>
<p>VENEZUELA	2.4050	 N.A.</p>
<p>N.A. - Not Available</p>
